[493.998687, "o", "# Cortensor Hackathon #5 - OpenMinion Core Building Blocks\r\nSource: https://docs.cortensor.network/community-and-ecosystem/hackathon/hackathon-5.md\r\n\r\n**Verdict:** do_it  |  **Effort:** medium\r\n**Reward:** $500 total, $250 liquid $COR upfront, and $250 in a one-month staking lock\r\n**Deadline:** December 18, 2026\r\n\r\n## Tasks\r\n- Create a functioning, reproducible agent\r\n- Explain and demonstrate the built functionality\r\n- Disclose external dependencies and keep secrets and private data out of public submissions\r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n- A submission needs a functioning, reproducible agent\r\n- Participants should be able to explain and demonstrate what they built\r\n- Participants should disclose external dependencies and keep secrets and private data out of public submissions\r\n\r\n## Red flags\r\n- none found\r\n\r\n**Why:** The campaign brief outlines a clear objective and submission requirements, with no red flags identified. The effort required is moderate, and the submission needs to be reproducible and demonstrate the built functionality.\r\n\r\n## Reviewer subagent\r\nAgrees: True\r\n- The evidence does not explicitly state that the hackathon requires a polished frontend, multi-agent system, or production deployment. The brief suggests that a simple agent that works reliably can do well.\r\n\r\nSaved to tracker: True  |  timings: {'brief_s': 284.9, 'review_s': 100.0, 'save_s': 103.7}\r\n\r\n"]
